7. COPYRIGHT AND STATUTORY RIGHTS

7.1 The Copyright Act, 1957 applies to AthleteOS to the extent the relevant material is protected by copyright and owned or controlled by Nova Code.

7.2 Section 14 of the Copyright Act, 1957 sets out the exclusive rights of a copyright owner, including specific rights concerning computer programmes.

7.3 Section 17 addresses first ownership of copyright, subject to its statutory provisions and applicable agreements or exceptions.

7.4 Sections 18 and 19 govern assignments of copyright and impose statutory requirements on assignments. A contribution or submission does not transfer copyright to Nova Code merely because it was submitted unless a valid assignment or other legal basis for transfer exists.

7.5 Section 30 permits licensing by a copyright owner or duly authorised person. Any licence granted by Nova Code is limited to rights actually owned or controlled by Nova Code.

7.6 Section 51 identifies circumstances in which copyright is infringed, while section 55 provides civil remedies for infringement. Nova Code reserves remedies available under those provisions and other applicable law.

7.7 Section 58 provides rights concerning infringing copies and plates in specified circumstances.

7.8 Section 63 provides criminal consequences for certain copyright infringement, and section 63B specifically addresses knowingly using an infringing copy of a computer programme in specified circumstances. Whether a criminal provision applies depends on the conduct and statutory requirements; this licence does not independently create criminal liability.

7.9 Nothing in this licence waives or restricts statutory exceptions under section 52 of the Copyright Act, 1957, including provisions concerning lawful possession of a computer programme, interoperability, observation/study/testing, and specified personal use where their statutory conditions are satisfied.

