13. USER DATA AND PRIVACY

13.1 This software licence does not grant permission to access, copy, disclose, sell, export, scrape, or otherwise process personal data belonging to AthleteOS users or other individuals.

13.2 AthleteOS may process athlete, coach, academy, administrator, or other user information as described in the applicable privacy notice and service terms.

13.3 To the extent the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and its rules are in force and apply to the relevant processing, processing must comply with the Act, including sections 4 to 10 concerning grounds and obligations for processing, notice, consent, legitimate uses, general obligations, children's personal data, and significant data fiduciary obligations, as applicable.

13.4 Sections 11 to 15 of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 address rights and duties of Data Principals, including access information, correction and erasure, grievance redressal, nomination, and duties. Nothing in this licence removes those statutory rights when the Act applies.

13.5 Section 9 of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 contains additional requirements concerning processing personal data of children. Where that provision is in force and applies, AthleteOS processing must be operated consistently with those requirements.

13.6 The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 was brought into force in phases by Government notification. The 13 November 2025 commencement notification schedules sections 3 to 17, among other provisions, for commencement eighteen months after that notification. References in this licence to those provisions are therefore subject to their actual commencement and applicability at the relevant time.

13.7 The Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025 are also subject to their notified commencement schedule. Where the Rules apply, AthleteOS must comply with the applicable provisions.

